WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.154
Maya Okafor: Alright, happy Friday everyone! Let’s get started. Quick round of updates—Lukas, want to kick us off?

2
00:00:08.437 --> 00:00:19.976
Lukas Brenner: Sure, thanks Maya. Not much from my side, just wrapping up some open enrollment questions for Germany. Oh, and I finally got a response from Allianz about the claims backlog.

3
00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:31.090
Priya Raman: Nice, Lukas. On my end, APAC is pretty quiet. I did get a couple of questions about the new leave carryover rules in Singapore, but nothing urgent.

4
00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:43.534
Daniel Ferreira: Hey all. I’m mostly heads down on comp benchmarking for Q3, but I did get a ping from Payroll about the Hungary dependent rates, so good timing on today’s agenda.

5
00:00:44.275 --> 00:00:53.890
Tomás Rivera: Morning, everyone. Legal’s all clear, just a heads up that we’ll need to update the privacy language in the handbook soon, but not for today.

6
00:00:54.359 --> 00:01:00.128
Maya Okafor: Thanks, Tomás. I’ll add that to next week’s agenda. Anything else before we jump in?

7
00:01:00.874 --> 00:01:06.644
Priya Raman: Oh, just a quick one—has anyone heard if the new wellness vendor is live yet?

8
00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:14.943
Lukas Brenner: Not yet, Priya. I think they’re still sorting out the SSO integration. I’ll check with IT after this.

9
00:01:15.902 --> 00:01:25.518
Maya Okafor: Alright, let’s move to the main item: the handbook policy changes for Italy, Hungary, and Luxembourg. Everyone had a chance to review the draft text?

10
00:01:26.622 --> 00:01:33.930
Daniel Ferreira: Yep, I went through it. The new dependent rates are all in USD, right? Just confirming for payroll mapping.

11
00:01:35.243 --> 00:01:43.320
Lukas Brenner: Yes, Daniel, all USD. The rates are effective May 1st, so we’ll need to flag that for anyone onboarding before then.

12
00:01:44.515 --> 00:01:51.823
Priya Raman: I noticed the resource links are changing to the Benefits Directory for Italy and Luxembourg. Is that live already?

13
00:01:52.518 --> 00:02:00.979
Maya Okafor: Good catch, Priya. Yes, the Benefits Directory is live as of last week. We’re moving away from the old Google Drive guides.

14
00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:09.264
Tomás Rivera: Just to clarify, the enrollment window language stays the same? I know we had some legal back-and-forth on that last quarter.

15
00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:14.536
Maya Okafor: Correct, Tomás. No changes there—still 30 days from start, with exceptions case-by-case.

16
00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:25.716
Daniel Ferreira: One thing—on the Hungary page, do we need to mention the payroll deduction timing for dependents? I think we got a question about that last month.

17
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:33.949
Lukas Brenner: Hmm, it’s not in the current draft. Should I add a line about deductions happening monthly in arrears?

18
00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:39.619
Maya Okafor: Yeah, let’s add that. Just a short note under Dependent Coverage.

19
00:02:40.363 --> 00:02:49.210
Priya Raman: And for Italy, do we need to specify that the Allianz rates are per person, not per family? I’ve seen confusion there before.

20
00:02:50.381 --> 00:02:55.766
Lukas Brenner: Good point. I’ll make sure it says 'per partner' and 'per child' for clarity.

21
00:02:56.676 --> 00:03:04.753
Tomás Rivera: No legal concerns from my side as long as the effective date is clear and the links are up to date.

22
00:03:05.737 --> 00:03:08.429
Maya Okafor: Great. Any other concerns before we finalize?

23
00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:10.839
Daniel Ferreira: Nope, looks good to me.

24
00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.824
Priya Raman: All good here.

25
00:03:13.591 --> 00:03:16.668
Lukas Brenner: Ready to update once we confirm the wording.

26
00:03:16.906 --> 00:03:29.598
Maya Okafor: Alright, decision: we’re approving the new dependent rates and resource links for Italy, Hungary, and Luxembourg, effective May 1st. Lukas will update the handbook pages and add the payroll deduction note for Hungary.

27
00:03:30.235 --> 00:03:31.773
Tomás Rivera: Sounds good. Thanks, Maya.

28
00:03:32.856 --> 00:03:38.626
Lukas Brenner: Got it, I’ll aim to have the updates done by the end of the month.

29
00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:47.813
Maya Okafor: Perfect. Last agenda item—quick note on the engagement survey results. Participation was up 12% this quarter, so thanks for nudging your teams.

30
00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:51.689
Priya Raman: That’s awesome! Any big themes we should know about?

31
00:03:52.496 --> 00:03:59.035
Maya Okafor: Mostly positive, but a few comments about benefits communication. I’ll share the summary doc after this call.

32
00:03:59.401 --> 00:04:04.401
Daniel Ferreira: Should we plan a follow-up session to go over the feedback in detail?

33
00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:10.025
Maya Okafor: Yes, let’s do that next week. I’ll send a poll for times.

34
00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:16.799
Lukas Brenner: Thanks, Maya. And I’ll make sure the handbook updates are highlighted in the next team newsletter too.

35
00:04:17.511 --> 00:04:19.011
Priya Raman: Thanks, Lukas!

36
00:04:19.945 --> 00:04:22.252
Tomás Rivera: Thanks, everyone. Have a great weekend.

37
00:04:22.487 --> 00:04:24.411
Maya Okafor: Thanks all, enjoy your weekend!

38
00:04:25.446 --> 00:04:26.946
Daniel Ferreira: Bye everyone!
